 "notes": {
  "alchemy": "Pay as You Go: $0.52 per million compute units for all usage and an 8% fee on gas sponsored on mainnet. On mainnet a PAYG team sponsors through Bundler Sponsored Operations (the onchain paymaster is Enterprise only): a sponsored send costs 3,000 CU, an estimate 500 and a receipt 20, so 3,520 CU an operation. BSO gas is \"the onchain settlement cost plus a BSO service fee\" that is not published, so every Alchemy price here is a lower bound and is never named cheapest.",
  "candide": "\"We never mark up the gas itself.\" Launch ($333 a month billed yearly, $399 billed monthly) includes 5,000 sponsored operations a month then $0.01 each, up to 100,000 user operations; Grow ($749 billed yearly, $899 monthly) includes 25,000 then $0.005, up to 500,000; Enterprise is from $3,000. The page shows the yearly price by default, and it is the cheaper, so it is the one priced; the monthly price sits in an attribute of the page that the drift check does not read. Starter's 1,000 sponsored operations are a lifetime allowance, not a monthly one, so it is not a plan here.",
  "circle": "Gas Station sponsors gas for Circle Wallets and invoices it with \"a 5% processing fee\". It works only with Circle's own smart-contract wallets, which bill per monthly active wallet past the first 1,000; that fee depends on how many wallets send, which this axis does not fix, so every Circle price here is a lower bound and is never named cheapest. Circle Paymaster, where the user pays gas in USDC, is a separate product and is not developer sponsorship.",
  "coinbase-cdp": "No plan fee: \"actualGasUsed × ethPriceUsd × 1.07\", a 7% markup on the gas, billed monthly. Gas estimation on CDP Node is 500 billing units, 10M free a month then $0.50 per million; one estimate per operation is counted, the most it would add. Base only. Coinbase also grants up to $15,000 of gas credits on application, which no bill here assumes.",
  "etherspot": "Pay-As-You-Go: $1 per 250,000 credits, \"Gas fees charged separately at network cost (no markup)\", from a prepaid deposit (a $10 minimum top-up). A sponsored operation is counted as estimate (300), sponsor (700), send (600) and receipt (25): 1,625 credits. A client that fetches paymaster data (450) instead of sponsoring spends less, so this is the most it would cost.",
  "openfort": "\"Paymaster calls\" are free and unmetered; broadcasting a transaction is 1 operation, so a sponsored operation sent through Openfort's bundler is one. The paymaster surcharge is 10% on Free and Growth, 5% on Pro and Scale. The Free card shows $0.01 an operation past 2,000, but a project without a paid subscription \"stops at the included limit\", so Free stops there. Openfort's v0.8 paymaster is not deployed on Ethereum, so delegated (EIP-7702) accounts there are not sponsored; smart accounts are.",
  "pimlico": "Pay-as-you-go has no monthly fee: 10,000,000 credits a month included, then $1 per 100,000 credits, and a 10% surcharge on sponsored gas on mainnets (`actualGasCost * 1.1`). Pimlico's own count is 1,050 credits per sponsored user operation (\"~9,500 if sponsored\" included, then \"~$0.0105 if sponsored\", against ~$0.0075 unsponsored). The Free plan is testnet only.",
  "thirdweb": "Growth ($99) includes 1,000 sponsored transactions, then $1, $0.60 and $0.20 per thousand at 100K and 250K, and a 2.5% gas surcharge on mainnet. Priced band by band; whether the lower rate applies to the whole count is not stated. The page lists 145+ chains without naming them.",
  "zerodev": "A user operation is 20 credits; mainnet sponsorship starts on Launch ($69, 100,000 credits) and Scale ($399, 1,000,000 credits), each with an 8% gas sponsorship premium. Wallet signatures (10 credits) are ZeroDev's signer and are not counted here. Overage past the included credits is not published, so ZeroDev is unpriced above 50,000 operations a month."
 },
